# Case of the Trampled Garden. Turn 1: Bot1 casts Grizzly Bears (Forest and Mox Jet), Llanowar Elves (Mox Emerald) and the
# Case (Black Lotus); the Case's enters trigger distributes its two +1/+1 counters one each to the Bears and the Elves (two
# targets, CR 601.2d: the Bears 3/3, the Elves 2/2), five power in all, so "To solve - Creatures you control have total power
# 8 or greater" does not happen at the end step. Turn 2: Bot2's Hill Giant (3 power) is on the battlefield. Turn 3: a second
# Grizzly Bears makes seven power for Bot1: one short, not solved - and Bot2's Giant, which would make ten, is not counted.
# The Bears attack with the Case unsolved: no trigger (Stack stays empty). Turn 5: a second Llanowar Elves makes exactly
# eight: the Case becomes solved at the end step. Turn 7: Bot1 attacks with the first Bears and the first Elves; the Elves
# that stays home is refused as the target, the attacking Elves are chosen: a +1/+1 counter (now 3/3) and trample until end
# of turn. Turn 8: Bot2's Giant attacks and the Case, Bot1's, does not trigger. Turn 9: the Elves have lost trample.

